From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:49:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-eip: support EIP96 extended replay windows

The vendor IPsec client rounds requested replay windows to hardware
encodings and treats every window above 128 bits as a 384-bit
record. EIP196 does not initialize those larger layouts, while
EIP197 cannot distinguish native 256-bit support from the 384-bit
fallback. This can silently weaken replay policy or produce an
inconsistent transform record.

Accept only exact EIP96 windows of 0, 32, 64, 128, 256, and 384
bits. Read the EIP96 OPTIONS capabilities, use the native 256-bit
layout when present, and otherwise reserve the 384-bit layout while
retaining the logical 256-bit context-update length. Reject unsupported
SAs before transform allocation.

Preserve outbound ESN when anti-replay is disabled and keep XFRM
eligibility aligned with low-level transform validation. The record
encodings and fallback allocation follow the EIP DDK SA Builder and
Linux 6.18 Safexcel definitions.

Link: https://git.codelinaro.org/clo/qsdk/oss/lklm/nss-eip/-/tree/10a89a95f814cd325e23105f102428644f45014f
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
